475:
(a) Each property owner or agent acting on behalf of the property owner shall be responsible for the normal care of trees located on its premises.
(b) Willful injury or disfigurement of any tree growing within the City shall be a violation of this article.
(c) No person shall:
(1) Remove any tree as defined herein without a permit, regardless of its condition;
(2) Attach any sign, notice or other object to any tree or fasten wires, cables, nails, or screws to any tree;
(3) Pour any material on any tree or on or near its structural root plate or critical root zone;
(4) Cause or encourage any fire or burning near or on a tree's structural root plate or critical root zone;
(5) Construct a concrete, asphalt, brick, or gravel sidewalk compact the soil, place fill material, or create other impervious or semi-impervious surfaces within the critical root zone of a tree;
(6) Pile building material or equipment on or near the structural root plate or critical root zone of a tree;
(7) Deny routine maintenance, watering, and reasonable arboricultural care to existing and newly established trees as may be required as a result of activities taking place under this section;
(8) Prune a tree in a way that is not consistent with ISA/ANSI A300 industry standard protocols, including but not limited to spiking or wearing spikes, spurs, or gaffs while pruning, cutting a branch below the branch collar, penetrating the vascular tissue during rigging operations, pruning more than 25 percent of the crown, removing a branch with a diameter that is greater than one-half the diameter of the main stem (trunk), making "topping" or "heading" cuts, or pruning a crown in such a manner that creates significant asymmetry;
(9) Remove a tree on a City right-of-way without written approval from the Director; or
(10) Operate equipment or machinery of any kind including driving over or through, grading, compacting, tamping, rolling, excavating or disturbing the soil in any way, including sod installation, within the critical root zone or structural root plate of any tree or stand of trees regardless of the existence or lack of an approved site plan. This includes during the site final landscape and stabilization phase.
(d) This article applies to the development of all property lying within the City, inclusive of property owned by the City, its agencies, authorities, and affiliated entities, except as otherwise provided in this article.
(Ord. No. 2021-06-03, § I(Attch.), 6-29-2021; Ord. No. 2022-10-01, § I, 10-25-2022; Ord. No. 2025-07-02, § 1(Attch.), 7-22-2025; Ord. No. 2025-11-06, § I(Attch.), 11-18-2025)

480:
All tree fund money is used in various capacities for the preservation, replacement, and management of the City's urban forest. Tree funds may be used for:
(1) The purchase and installation of trees in parks, rights-of-way and other City owned or leased property. This includes annual purchase of a defined quantity of trees provided to Brookhaven property owners by the Trees Atlanta Front Yard Tree Program;
(2) Maintenance of living City trees including mulching, fertilization, integrated pest management, and pruning, and excluding removal of dead trees or trees assessed to be in poor condition or structurally compromised;
(3) Promotion of a healthy urban forest;
(4) Ecological restoration projects; and/or
(5) Operational costs for the City tree nursery.
(Ord. No. 2021-06-03, § I(Attch.), 6-29-2021; Ord. No. 2022-10-01, § I, 10-25-2022; Ord. No. 2025-07-02, § 1(Attch.), 7-22-2025; Ord. No. 2025-11-06, § I(Attch.), 11-18-2025)

